[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2880507985","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106320#issuecomment-2880507985","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106320","id":2880507985,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rsRBR","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-14T14:41:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-14T14:41:30Z","body":"> The new constructor's arguments are completely different types from the previous constructor, but to Godot they are all \"JavaObject\" I guess.\n\nIt should be able to disambiguate from the actual Java classes. At least that is the intention of this code:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/09fcbb86459498985a910cdd1684844a1968dc96/platform/android/java_class_wrapper.cpp#L122-L134\n\nThis is in the part where it's seeing if a method is a valid candidate for the arguments that are passed, and it's checking that the Java object is an instance of the argument type. If the types don't match, it should go on to the next candidate.\n\nCan you share a minimal version of your code to repro